cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying preprint, please cite it as below."
title: "Hyphae v2: Hash-Chained Verbatim Quotation — A Verifiable Provenance Layer for Grounded Retrieval"
abstract: >-
  Hyphae is a cognitive substrate that answers retrieval queries by emitting
  byte-identical quotations of stored memory fragments over a SHA-256
  hash-chained journal, with no large language model in the cognition path.
  Its distinguishing property is verifiable provenance: every output span can
  be independently audited back to named, unaltered source fragments, with an
  external Ed25519 head anchor closing the chain-aware adversary. The
  accompanying preprint frames verifiable provenance as an addable layer for
  any extractive retrieval system, uses a trivial echo (and echo+journal)
  control to show that measured correctness and grounding are properties of
  verbatim quotation rather than of the system, and evaluates against 18
  LLM-based configurations across two corpora plus a minimal tamper-detection
  benchmark.
